:: F10 {"position":"25,275","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C (High PEPCK activity converting oxaloacetate to PEP)

You correctly identified <<print $_c>> of 1 correct answers.
You missed <<print $_m>> correct answers.
You selected <<print $_w>> incorrect answers.

**Missed correct answers**
<<if $_m == 0>>None<<else>>C (High PEPCK activity converting oxaloacetate to PEP)<</if>>

**Incorrect selections**
<<if $_10a>>* A (High PDH, low PEPCK)<</if>>
<<if $_10b>>* B (High LDH, low PEPCK)<</if>>
<<if $_10d>>* D (High citrate lyase activity converting citrate to acetyl-CoA)<</if>>
<<if $_w == 0>>None<</if>>

High PEPCK activity promotes conversion of oxaloacetate to phosphoenolpyruvate, directing TCA-cycle carbon toward gluconeogenesis and net glucose production. High pyruvate dehydrogenase favours oxidation, high lactate dehydrogenase favours lactate production, and citrate lyase supports lipid synthesis rather than glucose formation.

